// A fixed array as a struct field is refused, and must stay refused until the
// declaration carries its layout.
//
// `[T; N]` is a fixed-layout value type, so a struct field of that type is a
// legal inline member once the compiler can describe its size and alignment to
// every backend. Today the declaration is rejected outright, which is the safe
// side of the gap: no backend can build a layout for it yet. This case pins the
// rejection so the surface cannot open by accident; accepting it requires the
// field layout work and a positive test in the same change.
struct Lanes {
    lanes: [u8; 16]
}
print(1)
